                <pb facs="0587" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2415: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-10T09:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 10,
                                1919, 9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            September 10, 7.38 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have persuaded Minister of Finance that action suggested is desirable in the
                    interest of Chinese. He has today asked the old consortium whether or not they
                    will make an administrative loan under their reorganization loan option. He
                    expects a negative reply. If he can be persuaded to exchange notes he desires to
                    do it by way of making the American group the exclusive financial agent for
                    Government loans of all kinds. In my reply I should of course state that the
                    American group will understand that it may invite other national groups to
                    participate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
